# audio bundle — config ownership (deploy.sh SDK + w-reset).
# TSV: <path>\t<class>. Absolute path → config/root<path> (always managed);
# home-relative → config/skel/<path>. class: user = seed-if-absent, managed =
# overwrite (W owns it). A trailing '/' marks a directory tree.
#
# Ardour's two config files are seeds, the user's from the first start (Ardour
# rewrites both in full on exit). Each carries only what W decides:
#   config    — the JACK/Pipewire engine backend at 48 kHz / 256 frames (the
#               audio-device dialog opens on it, not on raw ALSA, which PipeWire
#               holds), and discover-plugins-on-start (VST3 — Surge XT — is
#               scanned at start, not only after a manual Plugin Manager scan);
#   ui_config — color-file "w": the colour theme the ardour axis renders.
# Ardour fills in every other option with its defaults. The path carries the
# major version (ardour9); Ardour 10 reads ~/.config/ardour10 — re-seed then.
#
# Deliberately NOT owned: the theme file itself (~/.config/ardour9/themes/
# w-ardour.colors — the ardour w-style axis), audacity.cfg (the audacity axis
# edits one key in it), sessions and everything else Ardour writes.
.config/ardour9/config	user
.config/ardour9/ui_config	user

# Window rule (Hyprland drop-in, require()d by hyprland.lua with a wildcard):
# sizes Ardour's media import and qpwgraph's file dialogs, centres Ardour's
# Preferences (audio.lua).
# w-pack reloads running sessions on install/remove.
/usr/share/w/hypr/rules.d/audio.lua	managed
